WEBVTT

NOTE suggested-adjustments: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.080
Where the suggested percentage comes from,

V0-2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.900
why it caps out, and when
you should override it.

V1a-1
00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:17.619
Current is the percent adjust Lynx
holds for the station right now.

V1a-2
00:00:17.719 --> 00:00:21.707
Suggested is what Spatial Adjust
calculated from this morning's scan.

V1b-1
00:00:22.247 --> 00:00:25.743
The gap between them is the change
you are being asked to make.

V1b-2
00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:29.617
Current and Suggested sit side by
side under the Adjustment heading.

V2a-1
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.660
A station well under target asks for more
water; one over target asks for less.

V2b-1
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:49.461
Station 3AP1 measured 27.6 percent
against a 54 percent target.

V2b-2
00:00:49.561 --> 00:00:53.527
That is the largest deficit on the hole.

V3a-1
00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.104
Several stations show
the same suggested value.

V3a-2
00:01:03.204 --> 00:01:07.691
That is the daily Max Amount cap:
once the required amount exceeds the cap,

V3a-3
00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:10.903
every station above it lands
on the same percentage.

V3b-1
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:15.741
If most of your course reads identically,
the cap is doing the deciding,

V3b-2
00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:19.570
not the scan. Raise Daily Max
Amount in Settings, Calculation,

V3b-3
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:23.040
or accept that the course is
being deliberately limited.

V4a-1
00:01:29.613 --> 00:01:33.571
The percent adjustment column is yours.
Type over the suggestion for a

V4a-2
00:01:33.671 --> 00:01:37.573
station you know behaves differently,
and the row is queued for push.

V4b-1
00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:41.141
The suggested value is
left untouched underneath.

V4b-2
00:01:41.241 --> 00:01:45.850
Editing queues the station when the
new value differs from what Lynx holds.

V5a-1
00:01:53.573 --> 00:01:58.273
The soil factor editor scales a station's
calculated amount by 1 to 200 percent,

V5a-2
00:01:58.373 --> 00:01:59.373
permanently.

V5b-1
00:01:59.923 --> 00:02:03.173
It is opened with Shift plus Alt
on the gear button in the toolbar.
